d/modern/surprising-facts-about-queen-elizabeth-ii-royal-family-crown-netflix-olivia-colman-claire-foy"}]}, {"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01KDqqPMRYwKTRg2tbgQJ4Hf", "content": [{"title": "when did julius caesar live", "url": "https://www.twinkl.com/homework-help/famous-figures-homework-help/julius-caesar/when-did-julius-caesar-live"}, {"title": "was julius caesar alive when jesus was alive", "url": "https://matrix.mtrx.poff.ee/post/was-julius-caesar-alive-when-jesus-was-alive"}, {"title": "how old was caesar when he died", "url": "https://dev.automeris.io/area/061/ozM/download__VwXLgn__HowOldWasCaesarWhenHeDied"}, {"title": "Julius Caesar Timeline", "url": "https://lifeofcaesar.com/timeline-of-the-life-of-gaius-julius-caesar/"}, {"title": "The Exact Age of Caesar When He Died—History’s Brutal Math", "url": "https://seo-service.chartlocal.com/?p=18546"}, {"title": "Dark Light", "url": "https://dev2.argenox.com/?p=9477"}, {"title": "YOUNG JULIUS CAESAR", "url": "https://www.csun.edu/%7Ehcfll004/Early-c.htm"}, {"title": "Julius Caesar", "url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20220502011904/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar"}, {"title": "Julius Caesar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Julius Caesar"}]}, "**Queen Elizabeth II:** Guinness World Records lists her reign at 70 years and 214 days, counted from her accession on 6 February 1952 until her death on 8 September 2022 As of her death on 8 September 2022, Queen Elizabeth II had reigned without interruption for 70 years 214 days. She was born 21 April 1926 and died at 96 years and 140 days passed at the age of 96 years 140 days. Another source gives 25,569 days for her reign at the Platinum Jubilee, which is consistent with the Guinness figure Elizabeth II had reigned for 25,569 days.\n\n**Julius Caesar:** Caesar was born in 100 BC and assassinated in 44 BC. Wikipedia gives his birth as 12 July 100 BC and his death as 15 March 44 BC, at age 55 Died 15 March 44 BC (aged 55) Rome, Italy. Ancient sources point to 56 instead. Plutarch's account is often cited as saying he had reached the age of fifty-six Caesar died, having reached the age of fifty six years all told.. The difference comes from Roman age-counting and uncertainty about his exact birth date, so reports range from 55 to 56."], "durationSeconds": 6.292121625, "searchCount": 2}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Gnph8LE9DD6boLBfKF3vx5", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
